Package: gRate
Title: Growth Rate Data Preparation, Quality Control and Spatial Bias Correction
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Loukas", "Theodosiou", email = "loukesio@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A preprocessing layer for 96-well plate reader growth curve
    experiments. Reads raw plate reader exports, maps plate layouts to well
    metadata, flags problematic wells (no growth, spikes, drift, late jumps,
    noise), estimates and corrects spatial artifacts such as edge effects via
    median polish, and exports tidy data ready for downstream growth model
    fitting with packages such as 'growthcurver' or 'gcplyr'. gRate does
    not fit growth models itself; it prepares clean, well-annotated data so
    those packages can.
